# Building and testing

Run `./compile.sh` from a checkout to build `./executable`.
The implementation uses Go 1.21 or later and only its standard library; there
are no modules to fetch or runtime dependencies on another task manager.
Git is used for the repository/history operations. Editors and URL handlers
are invoked only for the corresponding interactive commands.

Run `go test ./...` for the parser, task model, YAML, and ID-cache tests.

The implementation is divided into:

- `query.go`: argument grammar, contexts, and due-date parsing
- `task.go`: task metadata, filtering, transitions, and project reports
- `yaml.go`: task-file parsing and serialization
- `store.go`: repository persistence, local IDs, and Git history
- `render.go`: terminal reports and display formatting
- `main.go`: command dispatch, editing, and completion support
- `cli_text/`: embedded command help and static CLI responses

Task repositories default to `~/.dstask`. Set `DSTASK_GIT_REPO` to isolate data
when testing. `DSTASK_CONTEXT` supplies a read-only environment context.
Build products and temporary development artifacts are excluded by `.gitignore`.
